icant findings other than mild weight which we attribute to her overall health management efforts.\n\nShe continues to take naltrexone 50 mg, which has been effective in supporting her recovery. Her latest lab results, including a level of 242, that her metabolic control is stable. We emphasized the importance of continued adherence to her treatment regimen and lifestyle modifications.\n\nMarch 21, 2022\n\nMs. Gill came in with an ankle sprain. Her blood pressure at that time was 137/71, and her weight was 135 pounds. She had a known history of Al"
